NAME
    ssh-askpass - password-only OpenSSH askpass companion for ssh.lib.sh

SYNOPSIS
    ssh-askpass prompt

DESCRIPTION
    ssh-askpass is the bootstrap-integrated helper used by ssh_password.

    OpenSSH invokes the helper with one prompt operand. For a secret-input prompt,
    ssh-askpass consumes the invocation-owned one-shot IPC value identified by
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID and writes that password for OpenSSH.

    When OpenSSH marks the request as a confirmation prompt through
    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT=confirm, ssh-askpass refuses the request without consuming
    the password. Normal callers use ssh_password from ssh.lib.sh rather than
    invoking this command directly.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID
        Required one-shot IPC identity established by ssh.lib.sh.

    SSH_ASKPASS_PROMPT
        OpenSSH prompt classification. The value confirm is refused.

EXIT STATUS
    0   password delivered successfully
    1   confirmation request, missing or invalid IPC identity, or IPC failure
    2   invocation does not contain exactly one prompt operand

SEE ALSO
    ssh.lib.sh
    ipc.lib.sh
